1
00:01:45,208 --> 00:01:46,833
We're locked in again.

2
00:01:48,208 --> 00:01:51,166
- How do we get out?
- There must be a problem. Relax.

3
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:52,750
What about Keila?

4
00:01:52,833 --> 00:01:57,500
She was outside. She's not opening up.
That guy must've done something to her.

5
00:01:57,583 --> 00:01:59,166
Keila has a camera.

6
00:01:59,250 --> 00:02:02,708
Damián and Berlin must've seen everything.
Don't jump to conclusions.

7
00:02:02,791 --> 00:02:04,041
Jump to conclusions, Roi?

8
00:02:04,125 --> 00:02:05,375
That guy's the psycho

9
00:02:05,458 --> 00:02:08,625
who locked you in a cage with a dog
and dumped you in the river.

10
00:02:08,708 --> 00:02:10,000
He shot me in the foot.

11
00:02:10,083 --> 00:02:13,750
Keila ran him over,
and now he knows she's a thief.

12
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:17,875
And what a coincidence,
she was right outside the money cave.

13
00:02:17,958 --> 00:02:20,833
You see?
This is gonna end really fucking badly.

14
00:02:20,916 --> 00:02:24,000
The duke told him we're guests.
He won't touch her.

15
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:28,500
The light again.

16
00:02:29,333 --> 00:02:31,458
The door opens, the light comes on.

17
00:02:31,541 --> 00:02:34,625
The door closes, the light goes off.

18
00:02:34,708 --> 00:02:36,750
- Roi, look.
- What?

19
00:02:44,708 --> 00:02:46,625
Boys, get to work.

20
00:02:49,291 --> 00:02:51,000
Where's Keila?

21
00:02:51,083 --> 00:02:53,083
With Berlin. Everything's under control.

22
00:02:53,166 --> 00:02:57,666
- Work in here? What if someone comes down?
- Exactly what I said to Berlin.

23
00:02:57,750 --> 00:02:59,833
What if someone comes down?

24
00:02:59,916 --> 00:03:03,833
Risk is part of the beauty of our job,
but we've got an advantage.

25
00:03:03,916 --> 00:03:08,375
Someone's already been down
and left thinking everything's in order.

26
00:03:08,458 --> 00:03:10,291
He's in the kitchen, having coffee.

27
00:03:12,875 --> 00:03:14,541
He doesn't look worried.

28
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:19,833
I hope no one needs cash
in the next 20 minutes.

29
00:03:19,916 --> 00:03:24,541
So do I,
or you're walking out at gunpoint.

30
00:03:44,666 --> 00:03:47,958
I can't believe it.
Locked in again for the third time.

31
00:03:52,958 --> 00:03:54,166
It's sealed shut.

32
00:04:02,375 --> 00:04:05,416
I hid a camera in the chapel.
They're watching us.

33
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,750
Now we'll see
what's behind this armored door.

34
00:04:07,833 --> 00:04:12,416
- You have the ground-penetrating radar?
- Yep. And echolocation sonar.

35
00:04:13,166 --> 00:04:17,083
We'll build a 3D map
of what's behind the door.

36
00:04:19,333 --> 00:04:20,708
We've got a problem.

37
00:04:23,083 --> 00:04:24,291
The duke's coming!

38
00:04:30,958 --> 00:04:31,958
May I?

39
00:04:33,750 --> 00:04:35,666
I don't mean to interrupt.

40
00:04:37,583 --> 00:04:43,041
I'll just take 30 seconds of your time.

41
00:05:04,250 --> 00:05:06,500
She's so mysterious.

42
00:05:06,583 --> 00:05:09,166
Enigmatic, I'd say.

43
00:05:13,625 --> 00:05:18,041
You're very focused on the task at hand.

44
00:05:21,375 --> 00:05:23,000
Where are the others?

45
00:05:28,333 --> 00:05:30,083
Working for you.

46
00:05:30,875 --> 00:05:34,166
Procuring what we need
through their contacts.

47
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:37,708
<i>Thermal lances, vehicles, the usual.</i>

48
00:05:38,541 --> 00:05:41,875
Sewage and security systems.
Stuff like that.

49
00:05:46,791 --> 00:05:48,250
"Stuff like that."

50
00:05:51,791 --> 00:05:55,208
Do you have a plan?

51
00:05:57,541 --> 00:06:03,125
We can't wait to share it with you.
Just a few details to finalize.

52
00:06:05,666 --> 00:06:10,500
It's so exciting to be running
the heist of the century.

53
00:06:10,583 --> 00:06:15,250
Even hatching the plan
is a work of art in itself.

54
00:06:16,083 --> 00:06:20,708
I'm dying to hear all the clever details.

55
00:06:20,791 --> 00:06:23,916
We're still chasing
that game-changing spark of genius.

56
00:06:29,666 --> 00:06:31,958
Then I'll leave you to it.

57
00:06:32,041 --> 00:06:34,583
I came to invite you to dinner.

58
00:06:34,666 --> 00:06:36,333
9:30 p.m.

59
00:06:41,583 --> 00:06:47,000
If you need Samuel to take you
to a tailor or a boutique…

60
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:49,750
Of course not.

61
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:52,333
I pack for every occasion.

62
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:03,500
Quite the sense of humor.

63
00:07:03,583 --> 00:07:05,500
I'll see you later.

64
00:07:13,083 --> 00:07:17,208
That nincompoop is a problem.

65
00:07:18,833 --> 00:07:19,833
A problem?

66
00:07:21,041 --> 00:07:24,000
Didn't you see him checking our screens?

67
00:07:24,083 --> 00:07:29,375
How he's marked us and wants to know
our plan down to the last detail?

68
00:07:29,458 --> 00:07:33,291
He seems invested and excited.
A patron's enthusiasm.

69
00:07:33,375 --> 00:07:35,208
No. Make no mistake.

70
00:07:41,625 --> 00:07:42,916
He may play the fool,

71
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,708
dancing on a player piano
like a hallucinating monkey,

72
00:07:45,791 --> 00:07:47,666
but he's got a criminal mind.

73
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:49,833
He'll force us to rack our brains.

74
00:07:49,916 --> 00:07:53,708
Him snooping around
shows he's neither calm nor confident.

75
00:07:53,791 --> 00:07:55,416
So what do we do?

76
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:10,208
Design a brilliant plan to steal it
as if we truly meant to.

77
00:08:10,291 --> 00:08:12,750
A real, flawless plan.

78
00:08:12,833 --> 00:08:14,666
I'll handle it myself.

79
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:17,541
We make a plan and then <i>don't </i>steal it?

80
00:08:17,625 --> 00:08:23,333
Exactly. To blow that idiot away
with a masterpiece of thievery.

81
00:08:23,416 --> 00:08:27,625
Sit down and take notes.
Hack like your life depends on it.

82
00:08:27,708 --> 00:08:30,750
Get me the painting's
departure date from Poland,

83
00:08:30,833 --> 00:08:34,250
its arrival flight in Spain,
and the company transporting it.

84
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:03,291
What are you doing?

85
00:09:03,375 --> 00:09:06,125
There must be a spring.
Santos opened the door.

86
00:09:06,208 --> 00:09:07,708
A thief enters, and it shuts.

87
00:09:07,791 --> 00:09:10,541
There clearly won't be an obvious button.

88
00:09:10,625 --> 00:09:12,708
The scan's done. Let's go.

89
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:15,208
How do we get out?

90
00:09:17,333 --> 00:09:18,916
Right on time.

91
00:09:30,208 --> 00:09:31,333
Keila, guide us.

92
00:09:31,416 --> 00:09:35,000
Cooks are on the service stairs.
Come up the east wing.

93
00:09:38,041 --> 00:09:39,166
You packed suits?

94
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,541
Good evening, everyone.

95
00:09:46,625 --> 00:09:50,041
I spent all day thinking how to make this

96
00:09:50,125 --> 00:09:54,625
a soirée to remember.

97
00:09:54,708 --> 00:09:56,500
And bam!

98
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,833
Inspiration struck,

99
00:09:58,916 --> 00:10:01,291
looking at the candelabra
in the mauve room.

100
00:10:01,375 --> 00:10:04,958
So I thought, why not dine
like in the olden days?

101
00:10:05,041 --> 00:10:09,541
As they did in the 18th century
when this palace was finished.

102
00:10:09,625 --> 00:10:12,500
So, bathed in candlelight,

103
00:10:12,583 --> 00:10:16,166
I toast to your success,
which will be mine.

104
00:10:27,791 --> 00:10:29,250
The atmosphere's magical.

105
00:10:29,333 --> 00:10:30,458
Definitely.

106
00:10:30,541 --> 00:10:33,791
- It's the warmth of the candles.
- I love the scent.

107
00:10:34,458 --> 00:10:35,458
Thank you.

108
00:10:45,083 --> 00:10:49,708
Sorry if this isn't the right moment,
but I need to say something important.

109
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:56,375
These last few days, I've been distant.

110
00:10:57,541 --> 00:11:00,000
I found out Keila had an affair.

111
00:11:06,541 --> 00:11:11,208
What seemed like a casual fling
became something more.

112
00:11:11,291 --> 00:11:14,916
And it's still going on. Romantically.

113
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,291
Bruce, stop. Please.

114
00:11:17,375 --> 00:11:18,416
No, Keila.

115
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:20,541
Nothing to be ashamed of.

116
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:25,125
I don't want pity or misunderstandings.

117
00:11:27,583 --> 00:11:31,750
When I found out,
I was obviously devastated.

118
00:11:35,416 --> 00:11:37,333
But she said she loves me.

119
00:11:38,458 --> 00:11:40,958
That I'm wonderful. On another level.

120
00:11:42,125 --> 00:11:44,208
And she doesn't want to leave me.

121
00:11:47,416 --> 00:11:49,250
And I don't want to lose her.

122
00:11:51,708 --> 00:11:52,875
So…

123
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:56,000
Keila.

124
00:12:01,291 --> 00:12:03,708
Do you want the three of us?

125
00:12:08,958 --> 00:12:09,958
Three of us?

126
00:12:10,041 --> 00:12:11,708
Three people, Roi.

127
00:12:12,541 --> 00:12:13,541
Her,

128
00:12:14,666 --> 00:12:16,333
that guy, and me.

129
00:12:16,416 --> 00:12:19,625
Jesus. Could you be any more of a fool?

130
00:12:19,708 --> 00:12:21,000
You know what, Roi?

131
00:12:22,250 --> 00:12:25,500
I build. I don't destroy.
Something you can't do anymore.

132
00:12:29,416 --> 00:12:30,583
So, Keila?

133
00:12:36,833 --> 00:12:40,750
I'm overwhelmed. I may have tachycardia…

134
00:12:40,833 --> 00:12:43,041
My brain's not working. I don't know.

135
00:12:43,125 --> 00:12:46,875
Maybe we should ask the third party.

136
00:12:46,958 --> 00:12:48,375
We will.

137
00:12:48,458 --> 00:12:52,541
Over coffee or something.
But answer me now.

138
00:12:54,375 --> 00:12:55,375
Well…

139
00:12:58,416 --> 00:13:02,541
Maybe we could explore that.

140
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,041
Yes.

141
00:13:08,333 --> 00:13:10,625
Very well. A toast?

142
00:13:11,291 --> 00:13:13,791
- To the threesome.
- The threesome.

143
00:13:13,875 --> 00:13:16,083
Hell of a way to start dinner.

144
00:13:17,916 --> 00:13:21,375
You have a very modern crew.

145
00:13:23,750 --> 00:13:24,916
Right, darling?

146
00:13:25,625 --> 00:13:31,333
Yes. They really are
a breath of fresh air.

147
00:13:31,416 --> 00:13:34,375
We're more classic, aren't we?

148
00:13:34,458 --> 00:13:37,291
Can you imagine us in a triangle?

149
00:13:38,041 --> 00:13:40,500
- I don't know.
- Come on. Indulge me.

150
00:13:40,583 --> 00:13:44,625
Go with this air of freedom
that's entered our home.

151
00:13:44,708 --> 00:13:47,750
Or imagine, you, me,

152
00:13:48,541 --> 00:13:49,833
and a woman…

153
00:13:52,625 --> 00:13:53,875
from Scandinavia.

154
00:13:53,958 --> 00:13:57,208
- A striking threesome.
- Right.

155
00:13:58,416 --> 00:14:01,875
I pictured two men.

156
00:14:02,791 --> 00:14:05,708
You, my love, of course.

157
00:14:06,208 --> 00:14:09,791
And… I don't know, a man from Brazil?

158
00:14:10,416 --> 00:14:11,791
For instance.

159
00:14:11,875 --> 00:14:13,875
Damián, what do you make of this?

160
00:14:16,833 --> 00:14:21,458
In life, one must choose, duck or a swan.

161
00:14:21,541 --> 00:14:24,375
What does that mean?

162
00:14:24,458 --> 00:14:29,041
The swan is one of the few species
that's monogamous.

163
00:14:30,291 --> 00:14:31,291
And romantic.

164
00:14:32,625 --> 00:14:36,708
And the duck, of course,
is a promiscuous libertine.

165
00:14:36,791 --> 00:14:38,166
The more, the better.

166
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:41,541
Me? I'm a swan.

167
00:14:44,041 --> 00:14:45,208
A swan?

168
00:14:47,291 --> 00:14:49,375
You're monogamous?

169
00:14:49,458 --> 00:14:50,875
Absolutely.

170
00:14:52,791 --> 00:14:55,791
Though I can imagine
how fun it'd be to be a duck.

171
00:14:55,875 --> 00:14:57,500
No judgment at all.

172
00:14:57,583 --> 00:15:01,583
But for me, love is focusing on someone

173
00:15:02,750 --> 00:15:04,666
and savoring it.

174
00:15:06,416 --> 00:15:07,416
How interesting.

175
00:15:08,833 --> 00:15:12,375
And the leader? What do you think?

176
00:15:13,125 --> 00:15:17,791
If we can enjoy
the love of just one person

177
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:19,625
who fills us with happiness…

178
00:15:19,708 --> 00:15:21,083
Wine?

179
00:15:21,166 --> 00:15:24,333
…and someone else appears,
and we fall in love with them too,

180
00:15:25,750 --> 00:15:30,666
shouldn't we enjoy double that happiness?

181
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:38,166
I don't agree.

182
00:15:39,833 --> 00:15:43,125
I believe in communicating glasses.

183
00:15:43,625 --> 00:15:46,750
You can't have two full glasses.

184
00:15:46,833 --> 00:15:50,958
If one is full, it's because another…

185
00:16:02,166 --> 00:16:03,166
was emptied.

186
00:16:06,791 --> 00:16:10,208
Love doesn't need
two or three half glasses.

187
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:15,416
It needs one.

188
00:16:16,291 --> 00:16:17,750
Full to the brim.

189
00:16:29,708 --> 00:16:31,500
Have you seen the vintage?

190
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:39,375
<i>"Tomorrow. 8:00 p.m.</i>
<i>Dinner on your boat. For 500,000."</i>

191
00:16:40,875 --> 00:16:42,416
I love your white shirt.

192
00:16:46,208 --> 00:16:48,708
Please. This is unbelievable.

193
00:16:48,791 --> 00:16:52,250
Can someone explain
that dinner in the dark? Good God!

194
00:16:52,333 --> 00:16:55,000
You couldn't tell
the ragout from the truffle!

195
00:16:55,083 --> 00:16:57,708
It's just like something
you'd come up with.

196
00:16:57,791 --> 00:17:01,750
That bubble of decadent beauty,
the candelabra dripping wax,

197
00:17:01,833 --> 00:17:04,416
like some Lord Byron castle.

198
00:17:04,916 --> 00:17:06,333
Right?

199
00:17:06,416 --> 00:17:09,750
One, it wasn't my idea.

200
00:17:10,333 --> 00:17:14,541
Two, I want minimal contact with our mark.

201
00:17:14,625 --> 00:17:15,708
Get to work!

202
00:17:34,083 --> 00:17:35,750
Wait till you hear this.

203
00:17:36,250 --> 00:17:37,875
The duchess is going all out.

204
00:17:37,958 --> 00:17:40,750
While we were making photocopies
like amateurs,

205
00:17:40,833 --> 00:17:44,083
she was redesigning the label
on the wine we drank tonight.

206
00:17:46,041 --> 00:17:48,583
- I don't follow.
- She put the bottle under my nose.

207
00:17:48,666 --> 00:17:51,625
In the fine print,
I saw an invitation for a date.

208
00:17:51,708 --> 00:17:53,916
Faded, like an old label.

209
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,250
Same typography as the '96 Rioja.

210
00:17:57,833 --> 00:17:58,833
How cunning.

211
00:18:00,083 --> 00:18:01,541
And original.

212
00:18:01,625 --> 00:18:04,833
So, she sent you a message
printed on the label.

213
00:18:05,708 --> 00:18:07,458
Bold, isn't she?

214
00:18:08,666 --> 00:18:13,333
Glorious madness, right?
The adrenaline of love and danger.

215
00:18:13,416 --> 00:18:16,875
She asked me to wear a white shirt
if I was interested.

216
00:18:16,958 --> 00:18:21,791
They set the dress code,
so I couldn't go against protocol.

217
00:18:21,875 --> 00:18:24,791
She must've taken it as a yes.

218
00:18:25,583 --> 00:18:26,791
She's coming on strong.

219
00:18:26,875 --> 00:18:29,416
Yes. And you panicked.

220
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:34,250
It's the responsibility
as a member of the crew and as a man.

221
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:38,583
For everyone's sake,
I won't meet up with her.

222
00:18:38,666 --> 00:18:40,833
You stubborn swan.

223
00:18:41,791 --> 00:18:46,666
Dear friend, I'm afraid retreat
won't work with the duchess.

224
00:18:46,750 --> 00:18:48,583
Can't you see? She won't give up.

225
00:18:48,666 --> 00:18:51,708
This will blow up in our faces.

226
00:18:51,791 --> 00:18:53,541
So what do you propose?

227
00:18:53,625 --> 00:18:55,500
Go. Make her your best friend.

228
00:18:55,583 --> 00:18:57,833
Buy her ice cream. Talk about your mother.

229
00:18:57,916 --> 00:19:00,333
Nothing kills desire like that.

230
00:19:00,416 --> 00:19:02,041
And remember this.

231
00:19:02,125 --> 00:19:03,875
No kiss…

232
00:19:05,166 --> 00:19:06,541
no crime.

233
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:14,291
You two analyze the crypt scan data.

234
00:19:14,375 --> 00:19:17,416
I want to know what's behind that door.

235
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:29,875
May we come in?

236
00:19:30,458 --> 00:19:32,833
What is this adorable thing?

237
00:19:32,916 --> 00:19:38,083
This is Mandarin.
She could be good company for Pomelo.

238
00:19:38,166 --> 00:19:40,166
He's been jealous lately.

239
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:41,583
Maybe because of me.

240
00:19:41,666 --> 00:19:44,291
This way,
the four of us can go for strolls.

241
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,541
Come in. Close the door.

242
00:19:46,625 --> 00:19:49,375
Let's introduce you,
see how you get along.

243
00:19:49,458 --> 00:19:51,041
Hi, Pomelo.

244
00:19:51,125 --> 00:19:52,583
Here's a friend.

245
00:19:52,666 --> 00:19:53,833
Easy, love.

246
00:19:53,916 --> 00:19:55,708
Look how pretty she is.

247
00:19:56,208 --> 00:19:59,000
Look. Her name's Mandarin.

248
00:20:02,708 --> 00:20:06,958
Sorry if the doorbell
woke you up this late.

249
00:20:07,625 --> 00:20:08,750
No.

250
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:11,750
You have no idea how happy it makes me

251
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:15,541
to be woken by the doorbell
in the middle of the night

252
00:20:16,708 --> 00:20:18,375
and see it's you.

253
00:20:19,625 --> 00:20:21,625
Well, you two.

254
00:20:22,291 --> 00:20:23,708
Know why?

255
00:20:25,333 --> 00:20:31,000
Because when you texted me saying
that you were having dinner with the duke,

256
00:20:31,083 --> 00:20:34,041
the truth is,

257
00:20:35,125 --> 00:20:37,250
I wanted to come too.

258
00:20:38,208 --> 00:20:43,500
And I know… it made no sense for me to go.

259
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,333
You're gonna rob him. It's your job, but…

260
00:20:49,875 --> 00:20:51,375
I was still sad.

261
00:20:54,458 --> 00:20:55,875
Silly, right?

262
00:20:59,250 --> 00:21:01,541
And I think it's because…

263
00:21:04,625 --> 00:21:08,125
I'm more in love than I should be.

264
00:21:12,041 --> 00:21:14,541
So I want to ask

265
00:21:16,625 --> 00:21:18,041
what do you feel?

266
00:21:24,166 --> 00:21:28,250
- Sorry.
- Thieves at work. On call 24/7.

267
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Answer.

268
00:21:31,166 --> 00:21:32,416
One second.

269
00:21:41,208 --> 00:21:42,208
Cameron?

270
00:21:42,291 --> 00:21:45,000
<i>- We arrived in Saïdia yesterday.</i>
- Beautiful beach.

271
00:21:45,083 --> 00:21:50,083
I imagine the illustrious passengers
went on a Jeep tour in the desert.

272
00:21:50,166 --> 00:21:55,458
Exactly. They sent the crew ashore too.
They blamed an electrical problem.

273
00:21:55,541 --> 00:21:57,666
They said it'd take six to eight hours.

274
00:21:57,750 --> 00:22:00,541
<i>Only two sailors</i>
<i>and the captain stayed on board.</i>

275
00:22:00,625 --> 00:22:04,625
To avoid suspicion, I said
I wanted to visit Ras Kebdana.

276
00:22:04,708 --> 00:22:06,250
Will I have time?

277
00:22:07,916 --> 00:22:09,541
Why do you want to go there?

278
00:22:09,625 --> 00:22:11,708
My grandfather was from the Chafarinas.

279
00:22:12,208 --> 00:22:15,833
I read you can see the islands
from the cape's lighthouse.

280
00:22:15,916 --> 00:22:18,208
Then today's your lucky day.

281
00:22:18,291 --> 00:22:21,000
<i>I acted excited and hurried off.</i>

282
00:22:21,083 --> 00:22:22,583
<i>But I stayed and watched.</i>

283
00:22:23,416 --> 00:22:26,333
- They didn't see you?
- Not a chance.

284
00:22:29,875 --> 00:22:33,791
<i>I came and went with grocery bags.</i>
<i>Potatoes, bread, fruit…</i>

285
00:22:33,875 --> 00:22:37,416
<i>I'd reach the end of the pier,</i>
<i>dump it, and go back for more.</i>

286
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:40,625
<i>No one boarded to fix anything.</i>

287
00:22:40,708 --> 00:22:43,625
<i>But something did go aboard,</i>
<i>a pallet of Nigerian rice.</i>

288
00:22:44,125 --> 00:22:45,541
<i>That's the odd part.</i>

289
00:22:45,625 --> 00:22:47,750
<i>I searched the yacht's holds.</i>

290
00:22:48,333 --> 00:22:51,125
<i>There's rice, but it's from Valencia.</i>

291
00:22:51,208 --> 00:22:53,083
So where's the Nigerian rice?

292
00:22:53,166 --> 00:22:55,625
I'll investigate when we weigh anchor.

293
00:22:55,708 --> 00:22:57,333
Keep me informed.

294
00:23:14,916 --> 00:23:17,583
Want to know what I feel?

295
00:23:18,083 --> 00:23:19,000
I feel

296
00:23:20,458 --> 00:23:22,833
what a man feels

297
00:23:24,583 --> 00:23:28,291
who, at dinner with strangers, has been

298
00:23:29,750 --> 00:23:33,208
thinking of you every time love came up

299
00:23:33,291 --> 00:23:36,875
and couldn't get you out of his head
while trying to think

300
00:23:36,958 --> 00:23:39,666
about the security measures of a vault.

301
00:23:39,750 --> 00:23:41,583
And late at night,

302
00:23:41,666 --> 00:23:43,291
he kept thinking of you,

303
00:23:43,375 --> 00:23:48,458
so he thought of making
a midnight trip to La Milagrosa,

304
00:23:49,333 --> 00:23:51,958
a pet shop, to find

305
00:23:52,791 --> 00:23:56,666
the most beautiful rabbit in town.

306
00:23:58,458 --> 00:23:59,625
It wasn't easy.

307
00:23:59,708 --> 00:24:06,041
I had to look up the difference
between a buck and a doe, but I managed.

308
00:24:06,125 --> 00:24:11,958
Then I took a taxi
and arrived at your place at 2:55 a.m.

309
00:24:12,041 --> 00:24:13,583
And from that moment,

310
00:24:13,666 --> 00:24:17,375
I pictured myself climbing the stairs,
heart racing,

311
00:24:17,458 --> 00:24:19,500
ringing your doorbell, and…

312
00:24:21,541 --> 00:24:22,750
losing my mind.

313
00:24:32,958 --> 00:24:34,333
Just to see your face.

314
00:24:38,416 --> 00:24:40,208
So, back to your question,

315
00:24:40,291 --> 00:24:45,083
what would you say a man like that feels?

316
00:24:50,125 --> 00:24:51,250
I think…

317
00:24:52,791 --> 00:24:54,083
he's a little obsessed.

318
00:24:58,625 --> 00:24:59,625
And…

319
00:25:03,333 --> 00:25:04,708
also in love.

320
00:25:06,208 --> 00:25:08,375
Fiery love.

321
00:25:27,291 --> 00:25:29,291
I don't know if this'll work.

322
00:25:29,791 --> 00:25:30,958
She's beat.

323
00:25:37,916 --> 00:25:38,916
Are you tired?

324
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:41,708
Me? I've never felt less like sleeping.

325
00:25:41,791 --> 00:25:45,416
Great. Because we're going
to make our first plan together.

326
00:25:46,375 --> 00:25:47,666
What are we stealing?

327
00:25:48,250 --> 00:25:49,875
The <i>Lady with an Ermine.</i>

328
00:25:50,958 --> 00:25:52,458
You'll love it.

329
00:25:56,750 --> 00:25:58,708
I know this security system.

330
00:25:58,791 --> 00:26:01,416
The key can be up to 16 characters.

331
00:26:01,500 --> 00:26:04,250
Worst-case scenario,
I crack it in seven minutes.

332
00:26:04,333 --> 00:26:08,500
Strange he'd use something so flimsy,
given that gallery setup.

333
00:26:09,791 --> 00:26:10,791
It makes no sense.

334
00:26:10,875 --> 00:26:13,000
Maybe he values art more than his money.

335
00:26:14,500 --> 00:26:17,250
In there, he's got millions in used bills.

336
00:26:17,333 --> 00:26:21,916
I doubt a mind like his
would settle for this.

337
00:26:22,958 --> 00:26:25,583
Or maybe that door
doesn't need much security.

338
00:26:26,083 --> 00:26:28,375
Keila, the map is rendered.

339
00:26:31,958 --> 00:26:35,375
The data from the GPR
and echolocation sonar are downloaded.

340
00:26:41,708 --> 00:26:44,625
Rhythm, you either got it,
or you don't, baby.

341
00:26:49,583 --> 00:26:51,208
He knows how to move his hips.

342
00:26:51,291 --> 00:26:53,208
- Focus, Keila.
- Sure.

343
00:26:54,583 --> 00:26:57,125
Now we'll see
exactly what's behind that door.

344
00:27:00,875 --> 00:27:03,166
It opens onto a circular hallway.

345
00:27:03,250 --> 00:27:05,916
That's the antechamber
to the secret vault.

346
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:07,166
Like an igloo.

347
00:27:07,250 --> 00:27:10,541
The GPR indicates
it's made of titanium plates.

348
00:27:11,500 --> 00:27:13,541
Looks impregnable.

349
00:27:15,083 --> 00:27:17,000
- Odd.
- What's odd?

350
00:27:17,083 --> 00:27:20,666
Why not leave it in plain sight?
Why the hallway?

351
00:27:20,750 --> 00:27:22,625
Titanium didn't go with his decor.

352
00:27:22,708 --> 00:27:25,291
The snakeskin carpet is hard to match.

353
00:27:29,458 --> 00:27:31,208
It looks like a bullring, right?

354
00:27:31,291 --> 00:27:32,916
The bull-fighting motif again.

355
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:35,166
It could be a security ring.

356
00:27:35,250 --> 00:27:39,083
There isn't even a handle
on the inner vault's door.

357
00:27:39,166 --> 00:27:41,416
Or a hydraulic wheel
or anything to open it.

358
00:27:41,500 --> 00:27:43,500
And there's something even stranger.

359
00:27:43,583 --> 00:27:44,583
Look at this.

360
00:27:46,250 --> 00:27:48,625
Double-layer walls.

361
00:27:49,208 --> 00:27:50,208
See?

362
00:27:50,291 --> 00:27:54,708
Why build a cavity between steel walls?

363
00:27:55,208 --> 00:27:57,875
- That weakens the structure.
- Wait.

364
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:04,083
What did you do?

365
00:28:04,166 --> 00:28:06,583
I used colors to show different densities.

366
00:28:06,666 --> 00:28:09,875
Blue is oxygen.
Red is something with a different density.

367
00:28:09,958 --> 00:28:11,083
Probably gas.

368
00:28:11,166 --> 00:28:13,375
Gas? What for?

369
00:28:14,458 --> 00:28:16,375
Maybe it's a narcotic?

370
00:28:16,458 --> 00:28:19,708
Knowing the duke, it fits, but…

371
00:28:21,375 --> 00:28:23,375
I'd bet it's flammable.

372
00:28:23,458 --> 00:28:25,375
From those six ducts.

373
00:28:25,458 --> 00:28:26,541
Zoom in.

374
00:28:27,291 --> 00:28:28,916
What gas?

375
00:28:29,708 --> 00:28:32,083
Hydrogen, methane, acetylene…

376
00:28:32,166 --> 00:28:33,000
I don't know.

377
00:28:33,083 --> 00:28:36,833
You're saying the duke
built that ring to make a barbecue?

378
00:28:36,916 --> 00:28:38,208
Exactly.

379
00:28:39,125 --> 00:28:41,708
It's an Indiana Jones trap.
He loves those.

380
00:28:41,791 --> 00:28:44,416
Like that angel hand opening the crypt.

381
00:28:44,500 --> 00:28:48,916
So whoever goes in ends up gratinéed?
Like cannelloni?

382
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:50,458
What kind of madness is that?

383
00:28:51,125 --> 00:28:55,500
Anyone who gets in there, Roi,
has already entered the duke's palace,

384
00:28:55,583 --> 00:28:59,208
gone down into his chapel,
opened his crypt,

385
00:28:59,291 --> 00:29:04,625
walked on his snakeskin carpet,
and cracked his alphanumeric code.

386
00:29:05,208 --> 00:29:08,125
Death would be their just dessert.

387
00:29:08,208 --> 00:29:09,708
That can't be right.

388
00:29:09,791 --> 00:29:12,958
That gas should activate
a hydraulic mechanism or something.

389
00:29:13,041 --> 00:29:15,041
Doors close. Gas floods in.

390
00:29:15,125 --> 00:29:17,416
And you go up in flames.

391
00:29:17,500 --> 00:29:20,916
What is he?
A psychopath? A horror story killer?

392
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:24,125
We have no proof. I need to analyze it.

393
00:29:24,208 --> 00:29:25,666
I need to think too.

394
00:30:22,083 --> 00:30:23,541
What are you doing here?

395
00:30:24,958 --> 00:30:30,875
I couldn't sleep, so I'm wandering
around your palace, ruminating.

396
00:30:36,291 --> 00:30:37,291
Love?

397
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:41,291
Heartbreak?

398
00:30:43,666 --> 00:30:45,166
Work?

399
00:30:46,750 --> 00:30:49,083
What keeps you awake?

400
00:30:49,166 --> 00:30:52,000
Mostly work.

401
00:30:52,083 --> 00:30:57,208
It's a great challenge.
My mind's in overdrive.

402
00:31:03,833 --> 00:31:08,458
I know that spiral well.

403
00:31:12,416 --> 00:31:14,208
And I have a remedy that's…

404
00:31:15,833 --> 00:31:17,333
infallible.

405
00:31:19,416 --> 00:31:21,000
Come.

406
00:31:57,416 --> 00:32:00,125
My head's going to explode.
I need to lie down.

407
00:32:04,666 --> 00:32:06,333
I'll take this off and join you.

408
00:32:07,666 --> 00:32:09,791
Where's your dignity?

409
00:32:12,416 --> 00:32:13,416
You're pathetic.

410
00:32:13,500 --> 00:32:15,250
No, you're embarrassing.

411
00:32:15,333 --> 00:32:18,250
It's painful to watch.
You can't grovel harder, dude.

412
00:32:19,166 --> 00:32:21,125
And bringing up a threesome at dinner?

413
00:32:21,208 --> 00:32:25,375
In front of everyone?
So she couldn't say no.

414
00:32:25,458 --> 00:32:26,833
Fucking pathetic.

415
00:32:26,916 --> 00:32:28,833
What's pathetic, Roi?

416
00:32:29,333 --> 00:32:31,708
Saying how you feel,
no matter who's listening?

417
00:32:32,583 --> 00:32:34,250
No, Bruce.

418
00:32:34,333 --> 00:32:38,416
Inviting the girl you love
to fuck another guy in front of you.

419
00:32:43,958 --> 00:32:46,000
It wasn't a ploy.

420
00:32:48,166 --> 00:32:49,791
It's a philosophy.

421
00:32:50,291 --> 00:32:52,625
What philosophy?

422
00:32:52,708 --> 00:32:54,916
Love, Roi. Love.

423
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:59,000
Normal people are moved
more by love than hate.

424
00:32:59,083 --> 00:33:01,416
That's human nature.

425
00:33:01,500 --> 00:33:02,875
- Yeah.
- And you know what?

426
00:33:03,541 --> 00:33:07,375
I'm sure I'll suffer. Absolutely sure.

427
00:33:08,208 --> 00:33:09,208
But I have to.

428
00:33:09,833 --> 00:33:11,875
Who are you, Gandhi?

429
00:33:12,375 --> 00:33:14,791
A minute ago
you were a clown in an Elvis suit,

430
00:33:14,875 --> 00:33:17,833
goofing off to make her laugh.

431
00:33:18,333 --> 00:33:19,666
It worked, right?

432
00:33:20,666 --> 00:33:22,166
Bad news.

433
00:33:23,833 --> 00:33:25,250
The guy you're up against

434
00:33:26,958 --> 00:33:30,333
is a well-traveled photographer
and graphic designer.

435
00:33:31,666 --> 00:33:34,166
And a fucking paragon of sensitivity.

436
00:33:34,791 --> 00:33:35,791
Bruce.

437
00:33:36,791 --> 00:33:38,708
A clown can't compete.

438
00:33:42,083 --> 00:33:43,625
Listen.

439
00:33:45,416 --> 00:33:48,500
I made Keila fall in love
for the first time at 36.

440
00:33:49,666 --> 00:33:51,375
You know how, Roi?

441
00:33:51,458 --> 00:33:52,875
Talking about her muff.

442
00:33:52,958 --> 00:33:55,750
Whether she waxed. Stupid shit.

443
00:33:56,250 --> 00:34:00,666
Point is, she fell for a clown.
Not some intense, deep guy.

444
00:34:00,750 --> 00:34:02,791
So maybe, Roi,

445
00:34:04,333 --> 00:34:05,708
art is overrated.

446
00:34:22,375 --> 00:34:23,375
Here it is.

447
00:34:24,958 --> 00:34:28,583
My secret to stop the mental turbine…

448
00:34:32,333 --> 00:34:33,791
and anxiety.

449
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:40,125
Come, my love.

450
00:34:40,208 --> 00:34:41,541
Come.

451
00:34:44,791 --> 00:34:46,208
This is Prince.

452
00:34:47,375 --> 00:34:48,583
See? They talk.

453
00:34:50,333 --> 00:34:51,583
Touch him.

454
00:34:53,166 --> 00:34:54,500
That's it.

455
00:34:54,583 --> 00:34:56,000
Touch his mane.

456
00:34:58,125 --> 00:35:00,125
Talk to him. Let him know your voice.

457
00:35:00,708 --> 00:35:03,666
- How are you, Prince?
- Easy.

458
00:35:04,500 --> 00:35:06,291
- What is it?
- Hug him.

459
00:35:07,500 --> 00:35:08,750
Hug him.

460
00:35:08,833 --> 00:35:10,083
But…

461
00:35:10,166 --> 00:35:11,958
Go on. He won't do a thing.

462
00:35:12,458 --> 00:35:13,583
Like this?

463
00:35:14,500 --> 00:35:16,708
Not like that. Watch.

464
00:35:17,708 --> 00:35:20,708
Harder. Watch me.

465
00:35:23,416 --> 00:35:25,000
He has to feel your heat.

466
00:35:25,583 --> 00:35:30,208
When you hear his heartbeat,
feel your own.

467
00:35:31,458 --> 00:35:33,666
You'll see. They fall into step.

468
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:42,375
Now you. Do it.

469
00:35:51,791 --> 00:35:53,916
Focus on breathing.

470
00:35:55,708 --> 00:35:57,958
Sync yours with his.

471
00:36:00,375 --> 00:36:05,458
You'll see. Soon you'll both breathe
13 times a minute.

472
00:36:07,250 --> 00:36:10,208
Let him guide you. The tempo, the pauses…

473
00:36:12,708 --> 00:36:14,541
The depth of it.

474
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:18,875
Your body will start releasing oxytocin.

475
00:36:21,875 --> 00:36:23,208
And you'll feel

476
00:36:25,333 --> 00:36:26,958
extraordinary peace.

477
00:36:29,541 --> 00:36:31,541
I already feel it.

478
00:36:33,958 --> 00:36:35,708
Enjoy it, then.

479
00:36:35,791 --> 00:36:40,375
Because peace is going extinct,
like all good things.

480
00:36:40,458 --> 00:36:42,375
Isn't that right, Prince?

481
00:36:42,458 --> 00:36:45,416
And so am I.

482
00:36:48,708 --> 00:36:50,000
Pardon?

483
00:36:50,083 --> 00:36:53,583
Well, the haste,

484
00:36:54,458 --> 00:36:56,000
the phones,

485
00:36:56,583 --> 00:36:58,208
the ménages à trois…

486
00:37:00,833 --> 00:37:03,583
All of it will end the world
you and I belong to.

487
00:37:06,833 --> 00:37:08,708
I'm a swan too, you know?

488
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:16,125
We are…

489
00:37:17,833 --> 00:37:20,250
the monogamous horse whisperers.

490
00:37:24,375 --> 00:37:25,791
I don't know what to think.

491
00:37:26,875 --> 00:37:27,875
Neither do I.

492
00:37:29,875 --> 00:37:33,583
This conversation deserves a pairing.

493
00:37:35,250 --> 00:37:37,458
What are you saying?

494
00:37:37,541 --> 00:37:40,041
Nothing. I just want
to set a few ground rules.

495
00:37:40,125 --> 00:37:42,958
About this guy, Claudio.

496
00:37:43,916 --> 00:37:45,625
Here, Claudio is…

497
00:37:46,833 --> 00:37:48,041
the guest artist.

498
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:50,166
You follow?

499
00:37:51,250 --> 00:37:53,166
I know we're all learning, but

500
00:37:54,250 --> 00:37:56,750
I can't give you an inch
and have you take a mile.

501
00:37:56,833 --> 00:37:58,541
I don't want to take a mile.

502
00:37:59,625 --> 00:38:02,916
You're generous,
but I don't know how to handle this.

503
00:38:03,416 --> 00:38:05,583
I feel more maladjusted than usual.

504
00:38:16,458 --> 00:38:18,125
What if it's a bad idea?

505
00:38:18,208 --> 00:38:21,750
People are supposed to choose.
This feels selfish.

506
00:38:21,833 --> 00:38:23,250
Keila, relax.

507
00:38:23,750 --> 00:38:26,250
I only want to set a few boundaries.

508
00:38:27,708 --> 00:38:28,916
What boundaries?

509
00:38:31,458 --> 00:38:32,583
Well…

510
00:38:33,916 --> 00:38:37,416
Don't share an umbrella if it rains.

511
00:38:39,291 --> 00:38:41,000
No sharing ice cream.

512
00:38:41,083 --> 00:38:43,291
Or popcorn at the movies.

513
00:38:44,333 --> 00:38:45,625
One bucket each.

514
00:38:46,500 --> 00:38:49,125
No karaoke duets.

515
00:38:50,458 --> 00:38:52,166
I don't know, Keila…

516
00:38:54,416 --> 00:38:55,875
I'd rather you didn't…

517
00:38:56,916 --> 00:38:59,958
show him your virtual reality world.

518
00:39:04,208 --> 00:39:07,166
You said I was the only one
who'd seen it, Keila.

519
00:39:07,250 --> 00:39:08,750
Right?

520
00:39:12,041 --> 00:39:13,458
Or did you show him already?

521
00:39:29,583 --> 00:39:32,041
<i>Three Mauser shots</i>

522
00:39:32,125 --> 00:39:37,083
<i>You ran, jet black, saving my life</i>

523
00:39:38,250 --> 00:39:40,750
<i>What you did for me</i>

524
00:39:40,833 --> 00:39:46,416
<i>Horse friend, I won't forget</i>

525
00:39:46,916 --> 00:39:49,750
<i>I couldn't save you</i>

526
00:39:49,833 --> 00:39:56,625
<i>That bitter knowledge makes me cry</i>

527
00:39:56,708 --> 00:40:03,458
<i>That's why, you jet black horse</i>

528
00:40:03,541 --> 00:40:09,375
<i>I will never forget you</i>

529
00:40:14,750 --> 00:40:17,458
I'll tell you something
I think you'll like,

530
00:40:17,541 --> 00:40:19,000
although it may bother you.

531
00:40:19,083 --> 00:40:22,041
Go ahead.

532
00:40:22,541 --> 00:40:25,208
Unfortunately,
you are not becoming extinct.

533
00:40:25,291 --> 00:40:26,666
- You don't say.
- You're not.

534
00:40:26,750 --> 00:40:28,916
There are more specimens like you.

535
00:40:29,000 --> 00:40:30,125
- You saw them?
- Yes.

536
00:40:30,208 --> 00:40:31,666
- One moment.
- Yes.

537
00:40:38,916 --> 00:40:41,291
This conversation deserves a new wine.

538
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:47,000
A friend of mine is just like you.

539
00:40:47,708 --> 00:40:49,083
He's a sybarite,

540
00:40:49,583 --> 00:40:54,250
wine enthusiast, lover of beauty,
paintings, art…

541
00:40:55,416 --> 00:40:58,125
A Tuscan Chianti would be perfect,

542
00:40:58,208 --> 00:40:59,875
but in clean glasses.

543
00:41:01,625 --> 00:41:03,041
Your glass, sir.

544
00:41:03,125 --> 00:41:04,666
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

545
00:41:04,750 --> 00:41:07,833
So tell me.

546
00:41:09,333 --> 00:41:11,833
What else in your friend resembles me?

547
00:41:12,416 --> 00:41:14,333
He shares with you

548
00:41:14,833 --> 00:41:20,041
having a unique, personal
and immovable way of seeing the world,

549
00:41:20,625 --> 00:41:24,583
a universe of your own
where you arrange all other mortals.

550
00:41:27,250 --> 00:41:29,541
- Are you calling me egocentric?
- Yes.

551
00:41:29,625 --> 00:41:32,875
Of course. Narcissistic, egocentric.

552
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:36,041
But fascinating.

553
00:41:36,541 --> 00:41:39,250
A person who fills everything
with their presence,

554
00:41:39,333 --> 00:41:43,375
with a catalyst energy
that teaches you to enjoy life.

555
00:41:43,458 --> 00:41:47,041
And when you exit a room or a stable,

556
00:41:48,375 --> 00:41:50,375
the world seems empty,

557
00:41:51,250 --> 00:41:52,333
absent.

558
00:41:56,250 --> 00:41:58,166
And who is that friend of yours?

559
00:41:58,750 --> 00:42:00,750
One who's awake right now,

560
00:42:00,833 --> 00:42:04,166
looking for the spark of genius
for your robbery.

561
00:42:11,666 --> 00:42:13,083
Will he find it?

562
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:15,666
He always does.

563
00:42:17,583 --> 00:42:18,625
Always?

564
00:42:19,333 --> 00:42:20,708
He's infallible.

565
00:42:30,625 --> 00:42:32,541
I want to show you something. Come.

566
00:43:01,083 --> 00:43:02,500
Wait.

567
00:43:08,875 --> 00:43:10,375
Where are we going?

568
00:43:11,458 --> 00:43:12,500
To the chapel.

569
00:43:26,750 --> 00:43:30,000
All my forebears are buried here.

570
00:43:43,333 --> 00:43:46,041
Five generations of Hermosos de Medina.

571
00:43:49,916 --> 00:43:51,541
The twins are also here,

572
00:43:52,541 --> 00:43:54,166
Leopoldo and Armando.

573
00:43:55,083 --> 00:43:56,500
Four years old.

574
00:43:57,583 --> 00:43:58,708
A tragedy.

575
00:44:04,125 --> 00:44:05,750
Grab that little angel's hand.

576
00:44:06,791 --> 00:44:07,666
What?

577
00:44:09,833 --> 00:44:13,208
Grab the arm on that statue and pull down.

578
00:44:37,250 --> 00:44:38,416
You first.

579
00:45:16,875 --> 00:45:17,875
What?

580
00:45:19,250 --> 00:45:20,250
What do you think?

581
00:45:20,833 --> 00:45:24,541
Surprising decorations for a crypt.

582
00:45:25,458 --> 00:45:29,041
It's a crypt under another crypt.

583
00:45:29,125 --> 00:45:30,833
Another one of my secrets.

584
00:45:30,916 --> 00:45:33,416
Here I keep my third treasure.

585
00:45:33,500 --> 00:45:35,625
Would you be able to take it from me?

586
00:45:35,708 --> 00:45:37,000
The third?

587
00:45:37,083 --> 00:45:41,125
The first was the art collection
and you already trespassed it.

588
00:45:41,208 --> 00:45:42,208
Well.

589
00:45:43,875 --> 00:45:46,833
The second is my wife.

590
00:45:52,291 --> 00:45:53,291
And here…

591
00:45:57,083 --> 00:45:58,333
Here

592
00:45:58,916 --> 00:46:01,083
is my vault.

593
00:46:03,791 --> 00:46:07,541
Tell me, could you leave me with nothing?

594
00:46:08,625 --> 00:46:09,875
Well,

595
00:46:10,375 --> 00:46:13,125
everything's possible
in the art of thieving.

596
00:46:13,708 --> 00:46:14,625
The art?

597
00:46:17,541 --> 00:46:18,583
Turn around.

598
00:46:51,541 --> 00:46:53,208
You can turn around now.

599
00:46:57,000 --> 00:46:58,166
Ta-da!

600
00:47:01,291 --> 00:47:02,291
Go in.

601
00:47:22,750 --> 00:47:23,958
Don't you trust me?

602
00:47:26,875 --> 00:47:28,750
I don't know if this is appropriate.

603
00:47:29,333 --> 00:47:31,416
I'm telling you my deepest secrets.

604
00:47:31,500 --> 00:47:33,833
And now you won't trust me?

605
00:47:38,500 --> 00:47:39,875
Cross that line.

606
00:47:43,333 --> 00:47:44,666
Go ahead.

607
00:47:46,041 --> 00:47:47,250
Do it.

608
00:47:51,583 --> 00:47:52,583
Boo.

609
00:47:59,041 --> 00:48:00,208
Look at me.

610
00:48:03,791 --> 00:48:07,041
Do you really think
you could get this far by yourself?

611
00:50:42,125 --> 00:50:47,250
Subtitle translation by:
Soledad Etchemendy

